{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"12 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,9.257,3.651,3.268,"Cupid"],[13.889,14.731,38.406,2.373,2.124,"Guidance up a fourth time, margins down"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Cupid’s Q2 FY27 headline was strong: revenue of ₹188 cr, up 122% y/y, and"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"net profit of ₹56.2 cr, up 133%. The quality beneath it slipped. Other income"],[13.889,23.733,52.934,1.809,1.634,"included a ₹20.0 cr fair-value gain on investments; before it, pre-tax profit was"],[13.889,25.177,52.951,1.809,1.634,"₹52.9 cr, 12% below Q1. EBITDA fell 9% q/q to ₹54.8 cr on 21% more revenue,"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"as gross margin dropped 10 points to 48%: bought-in goods were 64% of H1"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"cost of sales. Cash fell from ₹186 cr in March to ₹17 cr, leaving net debt of ₹90"],[13.889,29.509,33.803,1.809,1.634,"cr after ₹225 cr of investments and ₹79 cr of capex."],[13.889,31.995,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Guidance rose a fourth time, to ₹880 cr of income and ₹275 cr of profit for"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"FY27 and ₹605 cr of profit in FY29, a 30-31% net margin throughout. We"],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"accept the FY27 revenue: the Palava plant starts in Q3 and two retail chains are"],[13.889,36.328,52.954,1.809,1.634,"being stocked. We differ on three points. 1) Margin: we assume 26-27%"],[13.889,37.772,52.934,1.809,1.634,"EBITDA against 29% in Q2, as traded goods gain share. 2) V2 Retail: ₹400 cr"],[13.889,39.216,52.951,1.809,1.634,"from 1.7 lakh sq ft is ₹1,960 a sq ft a month, 2.5x V2’s own ₹785; we take 60%."],[13.889,40.684,52.962,1.809,1.634,"3) Style Baazar: ₹200 cr is 11% of that chain’s FY26 sales, and Cupid is paying"],[13.889,42.128,52.964,1.809,1.634,"₹332 cr for c.12% of it. EQe profit is ₹197 cr, ₹211 cr and ₹261 cr for FY27-"],[13.889,43.572,19.741,1.809,1.634,"29E, 28-57% below guidance."],[13.889,46.034,52.936,1.809,1.634,"At ₹357 Cupid is valued at ₹48,004 cr: 283x trailing earnings and 79x the profit"],[13.889,47.502,52.959,1.809,1.634,"guided for FY29. Our Dec-27 target of ₹90 applies 47x, the highest forward P/E"],[13.889,48.946,52.964,1.809,1.634,"among ten Indian consumer peers (median 30x), to 12-month-forward EPS of"],[13.889,50.39,52.934,1.809,1.634,"₹1.85, plus ₹4 of investments. Granting guidance in full, the same multiple gives"],[13.889,51.834,52.931,1.809,1.634,"₹197, 45% below the price. We rate the shares Underweight (ladder: −5% to"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"+15%). Risks to our view: FY26 guidance was beaten, promoters added 1.7"],[13.889,54.722,49.918,1.809,1.634,"points to their stake in H1, and with no stock futures momentum can persist."],[13.889,57.21,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[16.248,66.579,0.509,1.022,0.915,"0"],[15.268,64.622,1.489,1.022,0.915,"100"],[15.268,62.665,1.489,1.022,0.915,"200"],[15.268,60.708,1.489,1.022,0.915,"300"],[15.268,58.751,1.489,1.022,0.915,"400"],[18.454,67.273,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[23.078,67.273,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.865,67.273,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.618,67.273,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.821,68.444,2.877,1.275,1.111,"Cupid ("],[21.701,68.47,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.314,68.444,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.398,68.444,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.566,69.604,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.803,69.604,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[29.998,69.604,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,69.604,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,70.67,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.095,70.67,3.363,1.387,1.209,"244.5%"],[24.547,70.67,2.597,1.387,1.209,"-2.5%"],[28.528,70.67,2.811,1.387,1.209,"29.0%"],[32.976,70.67,3.363,1.387,1.209,"604.9%"],[15.492,71.735,1.476,1.387,1.209,"Rel"],[19.095,71.735,3.363,1.387,1.209,"247.9%"],[23.996,71.735,3.148,1.387,1.209,"-14.6%"],[28.